<title>ECUADOR: Loans in default at Ecuador banks up 27.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Loans in default at Ecuador banks up 27.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuadorean banks held $405.8 million in defaulted loans in their portfolios in May, 27.5 percent higher than in the same month last year, the Central Bank said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Total bank loans were $4.11 billion, up 23.4 percent from May last year.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258429 x114</p>
